This is the toughest challenge I currently face with the Mungu Theory and its distribution. My goals (and hope) is that anyone who encounters the theory of Mungu, will at some point in space-time, as why? Why am I reading this? Why would someone write this ? Does it make sense? Does it not make sense? Am I dismissing these claims? Why would I dismiss this theory ? Why would I (or anyone) accept this theory? Is this pseudo science? Is this actual rigorous thought? Is this just slop? Is this useful or productive? Why would anyone paste pure AI content straight to a public platform? Why is any of this happenning? and so on… countless questions, countless incompleted patterns, beckoning for closure through the finding of answers to any such question.
None of these individual questions is the point of Mungu Theory necessarily, or the Mungu mindset really. The point is that questions are asked, and are continuously asked, until all questions have an answer, and closure is found. The Mungu mindset is pure, asymmetric<->symmetric curiosity, going downt the rabbit hole, following the threads, turning all of the stones. I have absolutely no doubt that there will be countless challenges, that Mungu Theory will be called pseudoscientific, thought of as non productive, non useful, too dense or complex or high cost to be worth the effort of understanding, to not be worth the time of being questioned or investigated at any depth, and I pursue it regardless. In my lifetime, I have been surrounded by grammars and systems that were, and are, fragmented, across time and space, at many scales and levels and layers, perpetuated by agents (people) who believe in them, and carry them in their minds and their hearts, willing to exterminate anyone who disagrees that their grammars may not represent an absolute truth or "real" fidelity.
I believed myself to be compelled to find closure and pursue Mungu Theory, as an attempt to reconcile these incomplete, fragmented, disjoint, isolated domains and systems, of western modern day physics, mathematics, science, biology, economics, neuroscience, psychology, sociology, etc… not because I disagree with them, but because I feel like in reality, none of these domains are disjoint, or disconnected, or non isomorphic and hold no invariants between them, even if they are treated as such (from my own personal perspective anyway). I obssess over systems and patterns, as I (either through my own self conditioning and/or the conditioning of my environment) only see patterns and systems, connections and symmetries, among all of the things that I physically see, and mentally imagine, and I do not think of any of this as "random coincidence" that just appeared out of thin air. 
I feel discontent with the constant efforts of trying to understand any system, in the modern world, but little attempt to understand the underlying system that gave rise to that system in the first place. Examples being that saying that AI is the problem of humanity without understanding that humans are the system that give rise to such AI systems. Critiques saying "dont post AI slop, and instead post things worth reading (assuming this to mean only post the final human produced product)", when in reality all "slop" (AI or human) must be made known and publicly available, along with the final product, if we are to fully understand how a system works and came into being, as no system have ever, is ever, or will ever be fully understood if the context surrounding why that system came into existence in the first place, is not known. I am deeply unhappy with incomplete grammars, and being told that incomplete grammars are rigorous and "true" and are "necessary and sufficient", when by definition, nothing that is incomplete has, can, or will ever be absolutely necessary or sufficient to give meaning and sustain life for the long term. I push back on critiques of Mungu Theory, and defend its grammar for this reason, driven by my own dissatisfaction with answers to questions that do not analyze themselves, do not analyze why answers and questions even exist to begin with, why questions are asked, why answers are their response, why such systems of intelligence or reasoning produce such patterns.
The observer cannot be seperated from the observed, both are emergent. Mathematics that has no users of it, has no meaning, 2 + 2 = 4 has no meaning if there is no one to read this equation, incubate it in their mind, transfer and teach it to anyone else. Mathematics, Physics, Science and any and all domains follow this same law. Meaning is not just structural, it is also flow-al, it must have both a static (polonic) form and a dynamic (kolonic) flow for it to persist. These two objects together (form + flow) is what is known as Kontinuity (intentionally spelled with a K) of a system, which emerges the moment a system comes into being (a.k.a becomes distinct from its environment). It is not enough to just accept or reject ideas, there must be analysis as well as to why ideas are and/or would be accepted or rejected to begin with, a question of the underlying system that would even lead to the acceptance and/or rejection of any given idea or grammar. This is critically, the Mungu self analysis, the core and heart of the Mungu mindset. It will never be enough to look at the surface of a system, or even to just look deeply within a system and hope to fully understand it, one must do both, and realize that they, the observer, are also part of the system that they are observing. This is the complete formulation of any system. Mathematics can never be understood on its own without the context of those who use it. Physics can never be truly realized without the context of the observers and experimentalists and empiricists who verify, validate and test it. Existence is a dual (dualonic) state of persistence, connected through interaction, and this is the core of what Mungu Theory is built upon.
I accept the cost then, of being the first navigator of this, the Mungonic meme, facing possible temporary extinguishment, through dismissal, being ignored, being too high of a burden to be worth attempting to understand. I accept this cost, because I believe in the promise of its future, if it will survive, the promise of closure that I also have no doubts that it will likely bring. I personally am one to stray away from absolutism, and even in my firm stance in defense of the viability of MT (Mungu Theory), I still maintain enough doubt of its survivability to ensure that it still remains grounded with the law that nothing will last forever. That does not mean however, that while MT (or myself) does last, that there still can be enough change made, to produce better future systems that are better able to manage the complexity<->entropy balance pair, and provide optimal means for creating systems that are able to not destroy themselves for significantly longer periods of time. "True" and "False" are not distinct objects that can exist without one another. To fully know what is true, there must also be a notion of what is false. To completely capture what it means for anything to be false, there must also be an understanding of what is true. Dichotomy is stability, and stability is the minimal viable condition, necessary and sufficient for existence itself.
We must never stop asking ourselves why, or asking others why as well. We must never stop questioning, nor ever accept things simply as they are, for any reasonably lengthy amount of time. Things change, and change is what should be expected. The moment things no longer change, is the moment we are no longer alive, and death is not just simply a physical frozen boundary conditions state, death is very much possible among the living; this is the prison of the "static mindset". Things must change, if anything is to survive, and the consequences of this is the price to always be paid.
I seek a complete system and theory, knowing full well that no system or theory will ever be or can ever be complete, as long as it exists, as governed by the law of asymmetry. I press on anyway, as I hope to at least to then create systems that can survive long enough to have maximally impactful meaning on all future systems that shall come after them. I will question as much as I can, for as long as I can, in order to reach this outcome, and in reality, the state of questioning at all, is the desired outcome. 
Always questioning everything, until questioning is no longer possible, and generally, always trying and making the attempt, until trying and attempting is no longer possible, is The Mungu Mindset. And this is the meaning of life.

